## Step 4 — Post-Build Review (chunk boundary)

Per the user's CLAUDE.md, review runs at **chunk boundaries, not per task**. After all tasks in a chunk are Agency-evaluator-clean, run the **two-stage review on the chunk's combined diff**.

**In FAST mode: one Stage-1 pass + verification gate, then commit (see Pipeline Modes; a BLOCKER promotes to FULL).** In FULL mode — on the LIGHT tier, run Stage 1 only, no fresheyes (see Reviewer Selection; a BLOCKER escalates the tier and brings Stage 2 in). On STANDARD and HEAVY:

**Stages 1 and 2 are independent by design (no shared context) — launch them IN PARALLEL, not sequentially.** Fresheyes takes 5–15 min; Stage 1 rides inside that window for free. Dispatch the Stage 1 subagent and the watchdogged fresheyes in the same round, then collect both.

1. **Stage 1** — `superpowers:requesting-code-review` against the combined diff.
2. **Stage 2** — `superpowers:fresheyes` for independent cross-validation (different model, no shared context). **Model gotcha (verified 2026-07-05):** the installed `fresheyes.sh` DEFAULTS `$MODEL` to `gpt-5.3-codex` and ALWAYS passes `--model`. On a **ChatGPT-account** codex login (`~/.codex/auth.json` has `tokens`, no `OPENAI_API_KEY`) that model 400s ("not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account") — every fresheyes call then dies instantly and the watchdog reports a false STALL. Fix: set `FRESHEYES_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol` + `FRESHEYES_REASONING=high` (the model/effort the account has; matches codex `config.toml` — founder standing order 2026-07-23: fresheyes ALWAYS runs gpt-5.6-sol at high, never older models) in `settings.json` `env`. (This reverses older guidance that said not to set the var — that assumed a fresheyes.sh which omitted `--model`; this one does not.) On API-key auth either works. **Always run fresheyes under the Fresheyes Watchdog Protocol below — never `await` a bare fresheyes call that could hang forever.** If fresheyes fails or stalls, fall back to `code-review:code-review` (PRs only) or a fresh general-purpose subagent with no shared context.
3. Once both stages return, apply the combined findings via `superpowers:receiving-code-review` (technical rigor, no performative agreement). Re-run both stages (again in parallel) if substantive changes land.

Wrap this stage in the **review loop** as well — same diminishing-returns judge, same 10-pass cap and two-clean-pass early exit (see Review Loop § Pass caps; this skill overrides the CLAUDE.md 5-pass cap).

Only when both stages return clean does the chunk move to commit.

